config BR2_PACKAGE_WAYBEAM
	bool "waybeam"
	depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_THREADS
	# Each arm names the family whose backend the makefile would pick for it,
	# because the driver packages themselves carry no family guard: the
	# star6e backend is built for every family that is not hi3516cv6xx, so
	# without this a tree with the SigmaStar driver enabled on another SoC
	# could select waybeam and get an encoder for the wrong hardware.
	depends on (BR2_PACKAGE_SIGMASTAR_OSDRV_INFINITY6E && \
		BR2_OPENIPC_SOC_FAMILY = "infinity6e") || \
		(BR2_PACKAGE_HISILICON_OSDRV_HI3516CV6XX && \
		 BR2_PACKAGE_HISILICON_OPENSDK && \
		 BR2_OPENIPC_SOC_FAMILY = "hi3516cv6xx")
	depends on !BR2_PACKAGE_MAJESTIC
	help
	  Standalone H.265 video encoder and streamer with one backend
	  per SoC: SigmaStar Infinity6E (SSC338Q/SSC30KQ) and Hisilicon
	  Hi3516CV610 (V5). Drives the sensor and encoder directly and
	  exposes an HTTP configuration API.

	  On Hi3516CV610 the backend compiles against the public
	  OpenHisilicon V5 headers, links the vendor MPP userspace
	  libraries and drives the sensors as userspace plugins it
	  dlopens by name from /usr/lib/sensors. This package builds
	  the IMX662 plugin from the waybeam tree, where it carries the
	  mode table and ISP seeds the backend was developed against,
	  and hisilicon-opensdk skips its own build of that sensor so
	  only one copy ships. The IMX335 plugin is built from
	  OpenIPC/openhisilicon by hisilicon-opensdk -- one source and
	  one pin. The vendor MPP kernel modules stay the ones S70vendor
	  loads at boot; the backend re-inits the graph around them and
	  never reloads them.

	  Infinity6C (SSC378QE) is not offered here even though the
	  encoder has a backend for it: waybeam's I6C backend targets
	  the 2024-06-18 SigmaStar MI libraries and
	  sigmastar-osdrv-infinity6c ships 2022-09-07. The pipeline
	  streams against those, but AE never actuates and the image
	  is black. I6C returns once the two agree.

	  It is an alternative to the Majestic streamer and cannot be
	  built alongside it: both drive the same sensor and encoder
	  hardware, so only one of the two can own the graph. On
	  SigmaStar they additionally share the OSDRV MI libraries,
	  which OSDRV installs only when Majestic is not selected.

	  Installs:
	    - /usr/bin/waybeam
	    - /etc/waybeam.json
	    - /etc/init.d/S95waybeam
	    - SigmaStar Infinity6E: /usr/bin/json_cli and unlocked
	      imx335/imx415 sensor modules, compiled here against this
	      board's kernel
	    - Hi3516CV610: libsns_imx662.so, compiled here (the
	      hisilicon-opensdk build of the same sensor is filtered
	      out, so this is the only copy); libsns_imx335.so comes
	      from hisilicon-opensdk

	  https://github.com/OpenIPC/waybeam
